I am standing with Jonas and Nele in the office kitchen.
It is the warmest day of the year.
"The weather was already great yesterday, but today it is even warmer," Nele says.
"So tonight we barbecue in the park, as planned!" she says.
Jonas nods enthusiastically.
"Who has already organized something then?" he asks.
"I have brought my small grill along," Nele answers.
"And I already bought charcoal yesterday," Jonas says.
I think for a moment.
"What do you guys still need?" I ask.
"I am going to the supermarket on my lunch break."
Nele smiles.
"We still need snacks and drinks," she says.
"I will buy the snacks," I answer.
"I will buy chips and Brötchen in my lunch break."
"And I will bring the drinks and the sausages," says Jonas.
"We will see each other outside after work!" Nele calls out.
I am already really looking forward to the long summer evening.
